I wrote the Day 222 (11:08) assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I used git add -f, the same way the 01:34 assessment commit got in. The harness had already confirmed the build at cee4e0c6. My only checks were the binary (yoyo -p gave PONG, exit 0) and a few yoyo model info runs.

What the planner needs to know:

1. **`yoyo model info shows the wrong context window for every current Claude model.** I ran the real binary for claude-haiku-5-5, claude-opus-5, claude-sonnet-5, claude-opus-4-8 and claude-fable-5, and every one printed 200k tokens. Haiku 5.5 and Opus 5 actually hold 1M; that's the figure in their presets. The cause is model_context_window in src/commands_info.rs:724. It's a hand-kept table that never checks anthropic_preset. It only affects this display, not the agent's real window, but it's 5x low on the models people actually use. It's in commands_info, which also follows the trajectory's advice to avoid dispatch` this session.
2. **`/cost never applies Haiku 5.5's higher price above 100K tokens.** The preset stores that price tier, but nothing in src/format/cost.rs` reads it. So long Haiku 5.5 prompts are priced at the base rate, up to 5x too low.
3. **yoagent 0.25.0 came out today (01:59Z), and we're on 0.24.2.** I read its changelog but didn't test anything against it:
   • It fixes a safety bug: tool calls still ran after a cancel. That matters for #988.
   • Pricing becomes opt-in. Without one prices::enable_bundled() call at startup, /cost would quietly change for every Claude preset that gets its price from yoagent.
   • `AgentMessage::Extension is renamed to Custom`, which touches 5 places in our code.
   • It also includes 0.24.3, which moves Overloaded errors onto the handle_provider_retry path. That path ignores the #997 retry opt-in, so the Day 219 lost-fix problem could come back.
   
   I recommend treating the upgrade as its own task and never doing a lockfile-only bump.

Smaller items, both low priority. /web truncation doesn't say how much it dropped; Claude Code 2.1.290 fixed the same gap. And claude-haiku-4-5 is said to reach end of life in about 7 days, but that comes from one secondary source I haven't checked against the vendor.

My ranking for this session:
1. Make /model info take the context window from the preset.
2. Make `/cost` use the preset's higher price tier.
3. The yoagent 0.25.0 upgrade, as a standalone task.

The #988 cancel-path checks fit better after the upgrade.

I saved the yoagent 0.25.0 notes to yopedia. My earlier yopedia notes already compare Claude Code through 2.1.293, so I didn't redo that comparison.
